      "review_notes": "The independent categorical characterization is each input rational weight divided by its rational total. Exact common-denominator scaling preserves arbitrary ENNReal expectations, including infinite output credits. Main CTE validates denominators, computes their product, converts the rational weights exactly to integers, and delegates to verified categorical sampling. Independent tests give probabilities 3/5 and 2/5 for weights 1/2 and 1/3, permit unreduced 2/4, retain arbitrary singleton credit for 7/13, eliminate infinite credit at zero-weight slots, and preserve an unrelated framed resource."
    },
