      "review_notes": "The exact finite-format law decodes an independent capped fair-geometric leading-zero count and uniform mantissa into an integer significand/exponent pair, returning(0,0) at the cap. It makes no continuous-uniform or IEEE claim. Fubini and the capped-geometric split supply one expectation identity. The CTE proof inducts on the remaining zero cap, draws a fair bit, then either advances the prefix or draws the verified random-bit mantissa and deterministic binary power. Independent precision 2/cap 2 tests give zero-output mass 1/4, point(4,-3)mass 1/8 and point(7,-4)mass 1/16; cutoff(4,-5)has zero mass even with infinite credit. Zero precision/cap, normalized infinite expectation and generic pair-valued framing are checked."
